#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Usage: class-overlay blank
       class-overlay pick
       class-overlay groups CHOICE
       class-overlay task [--pinned]
       class-overlay signal
       class-overlay choose TITLE OPTION...
       class-overlay noise
       class-overlay timer [--countdown]
       class-overlay dice [--sides N] [--remember FILE]

Full-screen overlay for the classroom tools, on the same monitor as the smartboard bar,
made to be used by touch alone.

pick:   A random student (class-tools pick-next), picked again in place.
groups: The class dealt into groups by CHOICE (class-tools groups-deal), shuffled
        again in place.
task:   The task for the class ("Arbeitsauftrag"), put together by tapping or taken
        from the prepared tasks in TASKS_FILE (blocks separated by empty lines).
        Shown big, or with --pinned as a small card in the top right corner.
signal: Attention signal, "Alle schauen nach vorne".
choose: Big buttons for the options, prints the tapped one. Exits 1 if cancelled.
noise:  Settings of the noise meter (class-noise): work mode, which also switches the
        microphone on and off, and its threshold, set on a live meter by dragging or
        by calibrating to the room.
timer:  Settings of the class timer (class-timer): presets, +1/+5 min, pause, reset.
        With --countdown just the time, as big as possible, for the class to see.
dice:   A die, rolled again in place. The number of sides can be changed there and is
        written to FILE for the next time.

Tapping outside a button or Escape closes the overlay. Only one full-screen overlay
runs at a time (PIDFILE, used by class-tools to close it), the pinned card beside it.
"""
